---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Backups & Export · Actuali"
  description="How Actuali creates, stores, and exports budget backups, and how to import them into Actual Budget on web or desktop."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6">
    <header class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Backups &amp; Export</h1>
      <p class="text-neutral-500">
        Actuali takes automatic backups so your finances are always protected on your device.
        This guide explains where backups live, how to export them to Files or your computer,
        and how to restore or import them into Actual Budget.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Where backups are stored</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        Backups are stored locally on your iPhone in Actuali's private app sandbox
        (within the application data container).
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        Because iOS isolates every app's internal files for security and privacy, backups do not
        appear directly in the iOS Files app by default. To access a backup archive outside Actuali,
        you simply <strong>export</strong> it using the share sheet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">When backups are created</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-neutral-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Automatic snapshots on exit:</strong> Actuali automatically captures a backup
          each time you leave or background the app. You never have to remember to back up before closing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Manual snapshots on demand:</strong> Open <strong>More &rarr; Connection &amp; Data</strong>
          and tap <strong>Back Up Now</strong> whenever you want to take an immediate snapshot before
          making large adjustments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Safety snapshots before restore:</strong> When you restore an older backup,
          Actuali automatically saves a snapshot of your live data first. A banner appears allowing you to
          <strong>Revert to Original Version</strong> at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Automatic retention:</strong> Actuali retains a rolling history of recent backups
          so you always have points to restore to without backups consuming unnecessary space on your device.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How to export a backup</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        Exporting allows you to save your budget archive to the Files app, iCloud Drive, AirDrop it to your Mac,
        or send it to another device:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-neutral-700">
        <li>Open the <strong>More</strong> tab and tap <strong>Connection &amp; Data</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Backups</strong> to see all available timestamps.</li>
        <li>
          Tap the <strong>Export</strong> button next to the backup you want to export.
          (You can also swipe left on any row or long-press it for the context menu).
        </li>
        <li>
          The iOS Share Sheet opens. From here you can:
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
            <li><strong>Save to Files:</strong> Choose any folder on your iPhone or in iCloud Drive.</li>
            <li><strong>AirDrop:</strong> Instantly beam the file to your Mac or iPad.</li>
            <li><strong>Share via Mail, Messages, or cloud storage:</strong> Send or archive the backup anywhere you like.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Importing into Actual on Web or Desktop</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        Actuali's backup archives are 100% compatible with upstream Actual Budget.
        Each export is a standard <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">.zip</code> archive
        containing <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">db.sqlite</code> and
        <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">metadata.json</code> with CRDT sync state stripped,
        exactly matching Actual's export format.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        To import an exported backup into the Actual Budget desktop app or web app:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-neutral-700">
        <li>Export the backup from Actuali to your Files or Mac.</li>
        <li>Open Actual Budget in your desktop app or browser.</li>
        <li>From the budget selection screen, select <strong>Import my budget</strong> (or go to <strong>Settings &rarr; Import backup</strong>).</li>
        <li>Select the exported <code class="rounded bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">.zip</code> file.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        Actual will load your full budget with all accounts, payees, rules, categories, and transaction history.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Restoring a backup in Actuali</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700">
        In <strong>More &rarr; Connection &amp; Data &rarr; Backups</strong>, tapping any backup timestamp
        prompts you to restore it.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-neutral-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Reverting:</strong> If you decide you want to return to the budget as it was before restoring,
          tap <strong>Revert to Original Version</strong> at the top of the Backups screen.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sync disconnection:</strong> Restoring an older backup deliberately detaches sync with your server.
          This prevents restored old transactions or deleted entries from immediately overwriting or conflicting with
          your server. To sync again, re-download the budget from your server (which replaces the restored local data).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
